[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649683116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113976#issuecomment-3649683116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113976","id":3649683116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Zib6s","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-13T18:18:02Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T18:38:54Z","body":"It looks like you have the angular distance set very high. I am able to fix the shadow in the MRP just by setting it to the value recommended by the documentation (0.5). Do you need it higher than that for your project?\n\nEdit: Screenshots with `light_angular_distance` = 0.5:\n\n<img width=\"1020\" height=\"700\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d6c5b0f-43e2-4b84-95ca-f479d85fbbaa\" />\n\n<img width=\"1020\" height=\"720\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31dd1610-b375-4328-a652-b1b8d8e0774e\" />\n\nAlso you have the directional shadow mode set to Orthogonal instead of using PSSM splits which will hurt shadow quality greatly unless you need it for an orthogonal camera.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649683116/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649717946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113976#issuecomment-3649717946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113976","id":3649717946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Zika6","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-13T19:05:53Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T19:05:53Z","body":"@KeyboardDanni I don't know that the documentation necessarily recommends 0.5, it just says that's the value for the sun from the earth. I specifically wanted to use a higher value for an underwater scene because regular sharp shadows look strange.\n\nAlso I set it to orthogonal to make debugging easier but it happens with PSSM enabled too.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649717946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649732613","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113976#issuecomment-3649732613","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113976","id":3649732613,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZioAF","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-13T19:24:36Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T19:24:36Z","body":"The problem with orthogonal shadows is that it will make your shadows very low resolution. To give you an idea, here's what you're working with at just 100 shadow distance with ortho:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d09ec55-0653-46d3-8b8f-a9129da862c8)\n\nThat's basically six pixels of shadow for the cube.\n\nAnyway, I went ahead and tweaked your MRP. How's this?\n\n[angular-distance-modified.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24145206/angular-distance-modified.zip)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5933e3a-b694-432e-9e63-2c409291e55d)\n\nThings I changed:\n\n- Set shadow pancake size to 0 (as it seems to interfere with PCSS here)\n- Set directional shadow mode to PSSM\n- Set light angular distance to 0.5\n- Set shadow blur to 4.0\n- Enabled blend splits\n\nIt artifacts a bit from a distance but I think it looks a lot better now. We can decide from there how to improve shadow blurring in Godot.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649732613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649871428","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113976#issuecomment-3649871428","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113976","id":3649871428,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZjJ5E","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-13T22:24:32Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T11:16:00Z","body":"@KeyboardDanni Your modifications do make the shadow look better, but unfortunately I am not willing to go that low with the `light_angular_distance`. I did figure out what the actual issue is though in regards to the rotation. The reason why rotating the plane causes the shadow to instantly appear + blur more depending on the angle is because PCSS is causing the plane to detect itself as a blocker and causes self-shadowing. I am able to increase the `light_angular_distance` a bit now without the described issue if I exclude the plane from the light's shadow caster mask.\n\nI will keep this open because this doesn't solve the root of the problem, I think that what should really happen is that each sample needs to be biased differently depending on the normal of the shadow receiver face and the distance from the center point to the sample point.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649871428/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]